### Initial Node Control
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-node-control.mdc#Control-Mechanics#Initial-Ownership
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Pre-Battle-Phase#Initial-state-setup

// Referenced by:
// - @battle-targeting-system.mdc#Initial-Target-Selection#Line-Restrictions
// - @battle-visual-feedback.mdc#Pre-Battle#Node-Display

Initial Node States:
- User-controlled nodes: 0, 1, 2 (permanent ownership)
- Neutral nodes: 3, 4, 5 (initially neutral, can be captured)
- Enemy-controlled nodes: 6, 7, 8 (permanent ownership)

Node Capture Rules:
- Only neutral nodes (3, 4, 5) can be captured
- Once captured, nodes:
  - Change ownership to capturing side
  - Update visual state to match owner
  - Can no longer be targeted
  - Become part of owner's network

### Network Lines
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Active-Battle-Phase#Network-Line-Movement
// - @battle-performance-standards.mdc#State-Updates#Movement-Tracking

// Referenced by:
// - @battle-targeting-system.mdc#Target-Selection-Rules#Universal-Targeting-Priority
// - @battle-visual-feedback.mdc#Network-Display#Line-Visualization

Line Properties:
- Lines connect adjacent nodes
- Movement only possible along these lines
- Lines serve as valid movement paths
- Lines cannot be traversed diagonally

Line Movement Rules:
- Battalions must follow lines exactly
- Movement speed determined by battalion stats:
  - Guardian: 9 units per second
  - Phreak: 7 units per second
  - Breacher: 5 units per second
- Distance calculation uses line path length
- Shortest path must be taken when multiple routes exist

## Movement Constraints
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Active-Battle-Phase#Network-Line-Movement
// - @battle-targeting-system.mdc#Combat-Range#Attack-Positioning

// Referenced by:
// - @battle-targeting-system.mdc#Retargeting-Logic#Target-Acquisition
// - @battle-visual-feedback.mdc#Movement-Feedback#Path-Display

- Battalions must always move along network lines
- Can only change direction at nodes:
  - Must reach a node to change lines
  - Cannot switch lines mid-path
  - Must stop at node to turn onto new line
- Can use any connected network line after initial attack
- Must maintain connection to network at all times

Remember: All movement must strictly adhere to these core rules while maintaining system integrity. 